{"id":"2b722e5b-f9a2-4020-8843-732613829d0a","body":"Follow-up from SMA-820: when this issue lands, review the "tool-result boundary" in the Gemini merge.

SMA-820 merges adjacent same-role contents. One exception remains: a `user` content with a `functionResponse` and a following user text stay two separate contents. The reason is that the translator sends no thought signatures. A merged `user[functionResponse, text]` keeps the call in the current turn, and Gemini 3 returns HTTP 400. The split shape gets HTTP 200.

When signatures are sent, the merged shape also gets HTTP 200 (probe shape 3, with a dummy signature). Then decide if the exception can go. See the section "Merge" in `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-20-sma-820-gemini-merge-same-role-contents-design.md`.","attachments":[],"createdAt":"2026-11-20T19:57:48.258Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-20T19:57:48.242Z","parentId":null,"resolvedAt":null,"quotedText":null,"author":{"id":"ba6021cb-56c5-43aa-9797-fab3599d7ead","name":"Sven Maschek"},"onBehalfOf":null}

